s=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs 75 years back to 1951, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids August to September came in under 90% of normal in 38 of them, more than any other pair. In 2025 the middle saw April to May at 140% and July to August at 77%. So far in 2026, January to February sat at 61% and June to July at 136%. Every grid had its driest year in 1964, with grid 26925 down at 60%.</p>"}
